    <!-- About / changelog -->
    <string name="about_title">Config Scanner v%1$s</string>
    <string name="changelog">v1.0.63
• Pipeline fix (review): a config that is UP but whose country cannot be detected now STAYS in the output as ❔ Unknown — healthy configs are never dropped just because geo failed
• Country results now need 2 providers agreeing; a single provider’s answer is never shown as a country (and ties are resolved deterministically)
• The plaintext-HTTP geo provider (ip-api.com) was removed — country data must not travel unencrypted
• Configs that cannot be parsed are now counted and listed in the Failed block with the raw line instead of silently disappearing (“invalid” counter added to the run summary)
• Thread-safety: the failed-reasons/process-log maps are now safe under high parallelism
• CDN ranges tightened: the huge Akamai/Google blocks removed (no more false ☁️ CDN)

v1.0.62
• CDN detection generalized: Fastly, AWS CloudFront, Akamai, Google frontends, Bunny/GCore (plus Cloudflare) — a tunnel that is up but geo-blocked now gets the ☁️ CDN label instead of disappearing as “no country”
• The label is provider-neutral: ☁️ CDN
• Unsupported protocols keep their clear skip messages (unchanged by design)

v1.0.61
• Reliability: the scan now runs as a foreground service — Android can no longer kill a long scan when the screen is off or you leave the app
• Port allocation rewritten: deterministic round-robin, no more random scan/collisions under high parallelism
• Hysteria2 YAML: full escaping of passwords/SNI/server (quotes, backslashes, control chars)
• Cert pinning no longer aborts on exotic SNI hostnames
• Code cleanups: leftover debug print removed</string>
